    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense faces a challenging slate today against a rotation featuring several tough arms, most notably the high-strikeout tandem of Chase Burns and Ben Brown. **Kyle Tucker** is our clear anchor, boasting a 69.61 efficiency score\u2014the highest on the roster\u2014driven by a favorable matchup against Roupp and his 4.07 xERA. While the team lacks an \"Elite\" 90+ rated play, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** presents our strongest high-leverage opportunity at 58.63. His score is bolstered by a +14% dynamic platoon advantage and a favorable wind forecast, which helps offset the significant negative impact of facing the talented Burns. **Andy Pages** also projects well (57.86), though his value is slightly tempered by the defensive efficiency of the opposing catcher, limiting his base-stealing potential in a category we prioritize above all others.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved balancing the thin margins between **Dominic Smith** (41.71) and **Heliot Ramos** (41.12). While both are technically \"Marginal\" starts, we are prioritizing **Dominic Smith** for his platoon edge against Brown, despite the latter's SP_xERA of 3.43. We are exercising caution with our remaining depth; players like **Gunnar Henderson**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill** are unavailable due to scheduling or rest, and **Luis Robert Jr.** remains on the IL, further thinning our options. We are monitoring the lineups for **Jordan Westburg**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Josh Lowe**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Nolan Schanuel** closely to ensure we aren't leaving points on the table if a late-arriving pinch-hit opportunity aligns with a favorable late-inning bullpen matchup. Risks remain high given the matchup against Burns, particularly for **Nasim Nunez** and **Brady House**, both of whom suffer heavily from the negative adjustment assigned to the SP's dominant skill profile.",
